WEBVTT

00:10.760 --> 00:12.095
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

00:16.016 --> 00:17.642
<i>We are the frontiers</i>

00:21.062 --> 00:22.814
<i>Confront with no fear</i>

00:22.897 --> 00:24.983
<i>From zero to a hundred in an instant</i>

00:25.066 --> 00:27.652
<i>Unveiling mysteries hidden</i>
<i>deep in the dark</i>

00:28.236 --> 00:30.196
<i>Even dead, I rise from the dust</i>

00:30.280 --> 00:32.741
<i>Reaching an unprecedented realm</i>

00:32.824 --> 00:35.035
<i>Trying your uniqueness</i>

00:35.118 --> 00:36.286
<i>It's a test level EX</i>

00:36.369 --> 00:37.662
<i>I'm the best, nothing less</i>

00:37.746 --> 00:40.206
<i>Pioneering from the east to the west</i>

00:40.290 --> 00:42.959
<i>Erasing all who resist, their data and all</i>

00:43.042 --> 00:44.210
<i>Did I really win?</i>

00:44.294 --> 00:45.503
<i>What are these tears?</i>

00:45.587 --> 00:47.922
<i>Who will be hated or loved</i>
<i>by the god of victory?</i>

00:48.006 --> 00:49.215
<i>To Each, their own wishes</i>

00:49.299 --> 00:50.300
<i>With friends, aiming for prize</i>

00:50.383 --> 00:52.343
<i>Seeking answers,</i>
<i>cutting through the unknown</i>

00:52.427 --> 00:53.678
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

00:53.762 --> 00:56.097
<i>Bugged out world, I'm a survivor</i>

00:56.181 --> 00:58.475
<i>Blazing with the guiding fire</i>

00:58.558 --> 01:00.310
<i>Show me the Show me the Shangri-La</i>

01:00.393 --> 01:01.436
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

01:01.519 --> 01:02.812
<i>Show me the Show me the Shangri-La</i>

01:02.896 --> 01:03.730
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

01:03.813 --> 01:06.691
<i>Declare war. At the system, we aim back</i>

01:06.775 --> 01:09.110
<i>Lose yourself, and it's game over</i>

01:09.194 --> 01:10.987
<i>Show me the Show me the Shangri-La</i>

01:11.071 --> 01:11.905
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

01:11.988 --> 01:13.281
<i>Show me the Show me the Shangri-La</i>

01:13.364 --> 01:14.699
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

01:18.703 --> 01:20.121
<i>We are the frontiers</i>

01:23.833 --> 01:25.335
<i>Confront with no fear</i>

01:26.252 --> 01:27.462
<i>You know I'll be there</i>

01:27.545 --> 01:28.713
<i>Overturning limits</i>

01:28.797 --> 01:30.507
<i>Now is the new beginning</i>

01:32.926 --> 01:35.220
As the clear sky transitioned…

01:35.303 --> 01:37.889
…into my ultimate strike, Heaven Bravo.

01:39.808 --> 01:43.603
So my words now turn into praise.

01:45.730 --> 01:47.690
Bravo.

01:50.235 --> 01:52.403
<i>Going back in time a little,</i>

01:52.487 --> 01:55.865
<i>three days after defeating</i>
<i>Wethermon the Tombguard.</i>

01:55.949 --> 01:58.493
(Tearlight Lake)

02:10.338 --> 02:13.091
<i>Kei Uomi is a pro gamer.</i>

02:19.347 --> 02:21.141
I bet you're at your limit by now.

02:22.767 --> 02:25.520
Lifestide Lake Serpent!

02:28.606 --> 02:30.275
Whoa, you-

02:34.279 --> 02:35.864
Tough luck.

02:35.947 --> 02:37.115
You missed.

02:40.994 --> 02:43.371
Now, for the finisher!

02:45.248 --> 02:49.502
Spirit Fist: Red!

03:01.306 --> 03:03.850
Woohoo! Level up!

03:03.933 --> 03:07.312
That water snake is so damn persistent.

03:08.021 --> 03:10.648
Level 53…

03:10.732 --> 03:15.111
Now I'm back to around where
I was during the Wethermon fight.

03:15.194 --> 03:17.238
Although it had to be done to win…

03:17.322 --> 03:18.489
What's this?

03:18.573 --> 03:19.741
It's called Evil Force!

03:19.824 --> 03:23.745
I used it once before,
and it was awful!

03:23.828 --> 03:27.707
You will lose one level
every thirty seconds.

03:28.750 --> 03:31.628
What?! I lose levels?!

03:31.711 --> 03:37.133
I went through a lot to raise my level,
and that thing knocked it down to 20.

03:37.926 --> 03:42.013
Still, they sure are quite
a pain to fight solo.

03:44.140 --> 03:47.101
Every water spray has a hitbox,

03:47.185 --> 03:50.021
and drop items even got dirt on them.

03:50.563 --> 03:54.734
The amount of details
this game has is ridiculous.

03:54.817 --> 03:58.238
Even when you have the idea,
nobody would bother to do it.

03:59.197 --> 04:01.199
<i>SLF</i> engine, huh…

04:01.366 --> 04:08.373
<i>Sunraku's story wasn't the only</i>
<i>thing that made Kei Uomi play</i> SLF.

04:08.539 --> 04:09.749
What?

04:09.832 --> 04:15.296
<i>The latest installment in the</i> Galaxia
Heroes <i>series set to come out this fall</i>

04:15.380 --> 04:22.345
<i>was reported to be using the same</i>
<i>game engine as</i> Shangri-La Frontier.

04:23.471 --> 04:29.185
Galaxia Heroes <i>is a fighting game series</i>
<i>primarily featured in international tournaments.</i>

04:29.269 --> 04:31.312
<i>If a new game of it is coming out…</i>

04:31.396 --> 04:38.319
<i>…it will be the future battlefield for</i>
<i>Kei Uomi and other pro gamers.</i>

04:38.403 --> 04:45.159
<i>A place to learn about the engine in</i>
<i>advance, being a mix of fun and business.</i>

04:45.868 --> 04:51.416
In that sense, I figured Wethermon
would be a good practice for me…

05:03.636 --> 05:07.390
<i>Although his instant strikes</i>
<i>were beyond human level,</i>

05:07.473 --> 05:11.477
<i>the speed of his grabs seems</i>
<i>to be doable by human, if barely.</i>

05:12.145 --> 05:17.275
<i>I can use the high-level performance</i>
<i>in this game as a reference.</i>

05:17.900 --> 05:22.280
Like vertically maneuvering
Metius from <i>Galaxia Heroes</i>…

05:28.286 --> 05:34.459
<i>If I was the one who fought</i>
<i>Wethermon, and not Sunraku…</i>

05:58.232 --> 06:02.987
<i>…would I have been able to beat</i>
<i>Wethermon the Tombguard?</i>

06:07.867 --> 06:13.956
<i>At the very least, Pencilgon decided</i>
<i>that Sunraku was a better fit.</i>

06:15.333 --> 06:16.751
Even so…

06:19.504 --> 06:20.797
Whoa?

06:20.880 --> 06:22.507
So heavy!

06:22.590 --> 06:24.383
<i>Even so, I…</i>

06:29.806 --> 06:33.768
<i>…have never once considered myself…</i>

06:34.310 --> 06:36.729
<i>…inferior to them!</i>

06:36.813 --> 06:39.232
C'mon! Come out now!

06:39.315 --> 06:42.819
Lifestide Lake Serpent!

06:45.696 --> 06:46.697
All right!

06:52.662 --> 06:55.164
What? A crayfish?

06:59.168 --> 07:01.170
(Rare Enemy
Lifestide Destro-Lobster)

07:03.172 --> 07:06.175
I run into a rare enemy now, huh?

07:12.515 --> 07:15.059
Spirit Fist: Red!

07:19.230 --> 07:21.482
So hard!

07:21.566 --> 07:24.569
I should've guessed as much
if it's a crustacean.

07:26.946 --> 07:29.740
Come to think of it, Sunraku did tell me.

07:29.824 --> 07:32.243
Oh, right, Katzo.

07:32.326 --> 07:33.327
What?

07:33.411 --> 07:37.623
There's a crayfish-like rare
enemy here, so watch out.

07:37.707 --> 07:39.417
Crayfish?

07:39.500 --> 07:42.128
I only fought it once.

07:42.211 --> 07:44.839
But it was super tough.

07:44.922 --> 07:46.883
It was a formidable foe.

07:48.759 --> 07:51.846
It would've turned badly
if I didn't have Emul with me.

07:51.929 --> 07:55.099
We made it through thanks
to our perfect teamwork!

07:56.809 --> 08:00.563
The EXP I got from it was
totally worth it, though.

08:00.646 --> 08:02.064
Hmm.

08:02.899 --> 08:04.025
As for how to beat it-

08:04.108 --> 08:07.236
No need to tell me.
I'll figure it out myself.

08:07.320 --> 08:08.196
You sure?

08:08.279 --> 08:09.363
Yeah.

08:09.447 --> 08:14.202
It's not like I only have one chance
with it like with Wethermon.

08:14.285 --> 08:18.080
I wish we could've shown you.

08:19.832 --> 08:22.126
Besides, I'm…

08:22.793 --> 08:23.628
Whoa!

08:25.630 --> 08:28.716
<i>Kei Uomi is a pro gamer.</i>

08:31.552 --> 08:33.846
Hmph, I see.

08:33.930 --> 08:39.435
That means if I can beat this
thing on my first time, solo…

08:40.436 --> 08:43.356
…I can consider this my win, right?

08:43.439 --> 08:44.982
Sunraku!

08:49.403 --> 08:51.113
<i>"It's just a game"?</i>

08:51.197 --> 08:56.452
<i>To give all I've got and</i>
<i>seize the victory is my job!</i>

09:00.706 --> 09:05.711
I'll show the true power of pro gamer
Kei Uomi when he gets serious!

09:12.718 --> 09:17.723
(Meanwhile, at the Secret Garden)

09:29.151 --> 09:32.029
Setsuna… This stoppage time…

09:32.780 --> 09:35.324
I wonder how long I can keep this going?

09:40.329 --> 09:43.249
(Thirdrema)

09:43.332 --> 09:47.753
Well, well. If it isn't the leader
of the Wolf-Gang clan.

09:47.837 --> 09:49.922
Allow me to show you the way.

09:50.006 --> 09:53.301
Haha, so I can really get in
no questions asked, huh?

09:54.176 --> 09:58.139
<i>The price I paid for defeating</i>
<i>Wethermon was huge, after all.</i>

09:58.764 --> 10:01.517
<i>I at least need to procure</i>
<i>some decent weapons.</i>

10:02.059 --> 10:05.313
<i>Or else even making</i>
<i>money will be difficult.</i>

10:06.856 --> 10:13.863
<i>But I can't make any monetary transaction</i>
<i>until I pay my debt back.</i>

10:16.157 --> 10:17.325
Right this way, please.

10:20.328 --> 10:24.081
<i>That means I'm left</i>
<i>with just one recourse.</i>

10:25.958 --> 10:27.585
Hey, you!

10:27.668 --> 10:29.253
It's you, Pencilgon!

10:29.337 --> 10:31.005
What are you here for?!

10:31.088 --> 10:34.050
What I'm here for?
Well, this is a weapon shop, right?

10:34.133 --> 10:37.094
I'm here to look for weapons, of course.

10:37.178 --> 10:39.055
This is not <i>just</i> a weapon shop!

10:39.138 --> 10:44.101
We in Schwarz Vulf
invested money into this shop!

10:44.185 --> 10:49.190
Only <i>special</i> clients
we formed contracts with are allowed to…

10:49.273 --> 10:50.191
Oh, wait…

10:52.526 --> 10:57.281
Right. We formed an alliance
with you guys, don't we?

10:57.823 --> 10:58.783
Uh-huh!

10:58.866 --> 11:01.952
So I'm your special client!

11:02.787 --> 11:04.747
Why her of all people…

11:04.830 --> 11:09.835
Although it's all to defeat Lycagon,
our leader sure made a bold decision.

11:12.463 --> 11:16.842
Wow, is this player-made?
It's well done.

11:17.426 --> 11:22.431
I guess some poor destitute players sold
this rare weapon as a last-ditch effort?

11:22.515 --> 11:25.184
We all have our ups and downs, I guess.

11:27.895 --> 11:29.271
Hm? What?

11:29.355 --> 11:35.486
I'm posted here just in case someone
as unpredictable as you show up.

11:35.569 --> 11:37.321
What are you saying?

11:37.405 --> 11:39.782
I can be a good customer,
buying stuff here on a regular.

11:39.865 --> 11:43.828
Like I can trust someone who
sold out their own clan.

11:43.911 --> 11:45.162
Oh, Ashura Kai?

11:45.246 --> 11:48.416
We had a common interest
at that time, that's all.

11:48.958 --> 11:51.001
Besides, I didn't lie
to you guys, didn't I?

11:56.632 --> 11:58.801
(Mahni owned)

11:58.884 --> 12:01.554
<i>Even if I had to crush Ashura Kai,</i>

12:01.637 --> 12:05.266
<i>even if I had to use up almost all</i>
<i>the resources I had built up to now…</i>

12:05.808 --> 12:07.810
<i>…I wanted to make it happen.</i>

12:09.103 --> 12:12.106
<i>To give Wethermon the Tombguard</i>
<i>his last rites.</i>

12:12.815 --> 12:16.694
<i>That was Setsuna of</i>
<i>Bygone Days's final wish.</i>

12:17.653 --> 12:21.949
<i>That wasn't just another</i>
<i>mission objective for me.</i>

12:22.032 --> 12:25.411
<i>That was my whole reason to play</i>
Shangri-La Frontier.

12:26.704 --> 12:29.582
<i>And once I have completed it…</i>

12:30.291 --> 12:33.169
<i>She disappeared along with him.</i>

12:35.087 --> 12:41.302
What goal should I set for myself
to focus on in this game from now on?

12:44.346 --> 12:45.598
(Log out?)

12:48.684 --> 12:50.019
Should I just…

12:53.981 --> 12:55.733
Yeah, right.

12:56.609 --> 12:57.526
Hm?

12:58.235 --> 13:01.238
Um, then, I'll take this and this.

13:01.906 --> 13:05.034
Oh, I'll also take this
as backup, I guess.

13:05.117 --> 13:07.912
Whoa, can you even buy that much?

13:07.995 --> 13:10.122
They are all pretty rare finds, you know.

13:10.206 --> 13:13.417
Oh, you haven't heard from your leader?

13:13.501 --> 13:14.460
Heard what?

13:14.543 --> 13:20.424
Our Sunraku found the Unique Scenario
where you can fight Lycagon.

13:20.508 --> 13:21.467
What?!

13:21.550 --> 13:23.427
And in exchange for that information,

13:23.511 --> 13:27.264
your leader said she'll cover my tab
for this one visit.

13:27.348 --> 13:29.391
Are you serious?
No one told me about that!

13:29.475 --> 13:32.394
We only talked about it just now.
I'm sure you just missed the memo.

13:32.478 --> 13:34.522
Wait, I'll message her now-

13:34.605 --> 13:37.107
Well, the thing is Lycagon
only appears during the night,

13:37.191 --> 13:39.693
and there's also a bunch of
other factors like moon phases,

13:39.777 --> 13:41.987
star positions, and like,
planet position, Kepler's laws,

13:42.071 --> 13:45.282
and everything needs to be right,
so we're kind of in a hurry.

13:45.366 --> 13:48.577
So we need to move fast and
a lot of help, anyone's help,

13:48.661 --> 13:50.454
so I'm here to get some stuff for it.

13:50.538 --> 13:54.542
In short, we are short on time
and need these stuff right now!

13:55.167 --> 13:57.294
Huh? Who cares?

13:57.378 --> 14:01.006
You better be!
This is a really important matter!

14:01.090 --> 14:03.801
If we missed this scenario,
what would you do?!

14:03.884 --> 14:07.513
Can you explain that to
your leader, that Psyger-100!

14:08.889 --> 14:13.018
What have you done, you fool!
This was our big chance!

14:13.102 --> 14:16.105
I keep telling you that
Lycagon is our top priority!

14:16.188 --> 14:17.314
B-But…

14:17.398 --> 14:18.816
No excuses!

14:20.317 --> 14:22.403
All right, fine.

14:22.486 --> 14:26.699
She turns into a whole different beast
when Lycagon is involved, after all.

14:26.782 --> 14:27.700
There.

14:28.951 --> 14:30.202
Wonderful.

14:33.664 --> 14:36.458
Well, just sit here and
expect some big news!

14:36.542 --> 14:37.459
Hey!

14:38.711 --> 14:40.087
How about I join you-

14:41.589 --> 14:43.591
She runs fast…

14:45.843 --> 14:50.973
Running into a player was a pain,
but anyway, I have my stuff!

14:51.056 --> 14:53.517
Now I can fight a bit more decently.

15:02.526 --> 15:06.739
And although I'm in a stoppage time,
I gotta have a goal.

15:10.910 --> 15:13.287
<i>Brooch of Faraway Prayer.</i>

15:13.954 --> 15:19.668
<i>This accessory she obtained as a reward</i>
<i>for defeating Wethermon…</i>

15:19.752 --> 15:22.671
<i>doesn't affect the stats…</i>

15:23.422 --> 15:24.965
<i>…but simply pointing at the west.</i>

15:25.758 --> 15:29.470
And it's showing me something beyond.

15:30.137 --> 15:33.515
The only item directly connected
to Setsuna of Bygone Days.

15:34.433 --> 15:39.939
It should be safe to assume
whatever lies beyond is related to you.

15:40.981 --> 15:45.819
Even if it's not, I can't pretend
I never saw it.

15:46.403 --> 15:49.406
Okay! I've got a pile of things to do!

15:49.490 --> 15:53.869
First, I want to get my foundation
sturdy and power up the Wolf-Gang.

15:56.413 --> 15:58.874
Thirdrema Archeduke's castle…

15:59.833 --> 16:02.127
I've usurped the thrones before.

16:02.211 --> 16:05.839
Maybe I should try seizing
power legally this time.

16:05.923 --> 16:07.716
Hey, you! Pencilgon!

16:07.800 --> 16:08.634
Oh?

16:08.717 --> 16:11.762
You bastard!
I knew you were lying to me!

16:11.845 --> 16:16.642
Our leader said she heard nothing
about the Lycagon info or paying your tab!

16:16.725 --> 16:18.435
Oops, you figured it out.

16:18.519 --> 16:20.771
- See ya!
- Wait up, you thief!

16:20.854 --> 16:23.774
Aww, way to ruin my parade.

16:23.857 --> 16:27.027
I was planning to sweet-talk
Momo-chan to cover my tab later, anyway.

16:27.111 --> 16:28.904
It's the same thing, right?

16:28.988 --> 16:33.033
Shut up! I saw you smirking
while looking at the castle!

16:33.117 --> 16:36.245
Are you planning to storm the castle
with those weapons you stole?!

16:36.328 --> 16:37.746
Haha, of course not.

16:37.830 --> 16:41.875
I was wondering if I could beat up
the guards to hopefully score a job offer.

16:41.959 --> 16:44.378
What kind of idea of fun is that?!

16:44.461 --> 16:46.672
Fun, huh…

16:47.589 --> 16:48.590
Yeah.

16:49.425 --> 16:51.677
Bounty Hunters!

16:51.760 --> 16:54.930
We have a PKer who cried wolf over here!

16:55.014 --> 16:56.807
Haha, that's mean.

16:56.890 --> 17:02.604
I'm broke with debt, but I'm paying
for it, so I'm as clean as a whistle!

17:03.230 --> 17:06.859
<i>I'm still enjoying this game.</i>

17:07.651 --> 17:11.363
If you want to find your own roots…

17:11.447 --> 17:14.533
The truth behind the world…

17:16.326 --> 17:18.871
You must search for Bahamut.

17:18.954 --> 17:21.206
<i>I hear you, Setsuna.</i>

17:21.832 --> 17:24.126
<i>I'm not playing on a "stoppage time."</i>

17:28.505 --> 17:30.549
<i>From here on out…</i>

17:32.301 --> 17:34.178
<i>I'm stepping into the next stage!</i>

17:39.725 --> 17:42.144
(Present)

17:57.785 --> 18:00.162
<i>Lycagon's shadow has been defeated.</i>

18:00.996 --> 18:04.625
<i>It hasn't been that long</i>
<i>since Wethermon was defeated.</i>

18:05.292 --> 18:07.836
<i>I fear, again…</i>

18:15.052 --> 18:16.386
(Chinese herbal gastrointestinal medicine)

18:16.470 --> 18:19.723
But this time I have my medicine.

18:29.441 --> 18:31.068
<i>ID verified.</i>

18:31.735 --> 18:33.737
<i>Enter your code.</i>

18:35.572 --> 18:36.907
<i>Code verified.</i>

18:37.741 --> 18:39.368
<i>Enter your fingerprints.</i>

18:40.828 --> 18:42.329
<i>Fingerprints verified.</i>

18:42.412 --> 18:44.540
<i>Performing retinal scan.</i>

18:44.623 --> 18:48.627
It'll be okay,
P.R. Director Sakai Tsuyomi!

18:48.710 --> 18:51.547
You can do anything when
you set your mind to it!

18:51.630 --> 18:54.007
You also have a strong stomach!

18:54.091 --> 18:55.467
<i>Retina verified.</i>

18:59.054 --> 19:02.141
You two, enough fighting!

19:06.228 --> 19:08.689
What is it? You look so desperate.

19:11.233 --> 19:12.568
What fight?

19:15.487 --> 19:17.990
Wh-Whose fault do you think…

19:18.740 --> 19:20.033
Forget it.

19:20.117 --> 19:23.287
Anyway, I heard that Lycagon's
shadow has been defeated.

19:23.996 --> 19:28.125
Her shadow doesn't impact
the World Story all that much.

19:28.208 --> 19:29.918
It's just a tutorial.

19:30.002 --> 19:32.546
No, even less, a prologue.

19:33.255 --> 19:38.093
It was defeated by the Attack Master
and two Marked players.

19:38.177 --> 19:41.013
Not a bad party to beat Lycagon.

19:43.557 --> 19:46.476
<i>Tsukuyo has a tendency to prefer</i>
<i>quality over quantity of players.</i>

19:46.560 --> 19:50.689
<i>And the higher the quality, the better.</i>

19:51.231 --> 19:55.068
<i>I suppose this means she has</i>
<i>no qualms about them this time?</i>

19:55.736 --> 19:59.156
And since you're not mad right now,
I suppose you have no objections?

19:59.239 --> 20:01.867
Are you picking a fight, pomade four-eyes?

20:01.950 --> 20:02.951
Poma-

20:03.035 --> 20:04.328
It's hair wax!

20:05.037 --> 20:07.956
Well, I got plenty of things to say…

20:08.040 --> 20:13.212
But Lycagon's shadow
has always been beatable.

20:13.295 --> 20:14.504
I have no complaint.

20:14.588 --> 20:16.965
I-I see.

20:17.049 --> 20:18.675
…or I should have.

20:18.759 --> 20:20.552
"Should have"?!

20:21.261 --> 20:25.515
But somebody…

20:27.267 --> 20:31.939
…apparently tried to silently
buff Lycagon's shadow.

20:32.022 --> 20:34.775
And she would've gone with it
if I hadn't seen the log.

20:38.570 --> 20:40.948
Yeah, obviously!

20:41.031 --> 20:42.157
What?!

20:42.241 --> 20:43.075
Whoa, hey-

20:43.158 --> 20:46.328
Lycagon is a smart creature,
so of course she'd prepare

20:46.411 --> 20:49.289
so she won't fall to
the same trick twice!

20:51.667 --> 20:53.126
Hey, wait.

20:53.210 --> 20:56.713
Don't just give her more
shadows on your own!

20:56.797 --> 20:58.048
You moron!

20:59.675 --> 21:02.261
You parasite!

21:07.140 --> 21:10.811
You haven't washed your hair
for days, haven't you?!

21:10.894 --> 21:14.523
I'll pluck all your hair so you
won't have to wash them ever again!

21:14.606 --> 21:17.818
Same for you! You didn't take a
shower again yourself, didn't you?

21:17.901 --> 21:20.279
I'll make your whole body smell
like deodorant and nothing else!

21:21.071 --> 21:23.949
I-In the end, it's always this, huh.

21:24.491 --> 21:27.286
No, this much is to be expected.

21:27.828 --> 21:30.289
<i>But I'm different from before!</i>

21:35.377 --> 21:37.796
Let's go, my stomach!

21:37.879 --> 21:39.631
I have plenty of ammo!

21:44.344 --> 21:49.224
You two are adults! You're not in
kindergarten anymore, so stop fighting!

21:49.308 --> 21:51.435
Stop fighting!

21:51.518 --> 21:53.687
Stop fighting!

21:53.770 --> 21:56.940
Get lost, you pomade four-eyes!

21:57.774 --> 21:59.735
(1 Damage)

22:02.779 --> 22:07.117
<i>The fight between Tsukuyo Tsukuri</i>
<i>and Ritsu Amachi continues on</i>

22:07.200 --> 22:11.496
<i>even after Sakai Tsukuyogi</i>
<i>ran out of his stomach medicine.</i>

22:31.475 --> 22:33.977
I hide in my brain every day

22:34.061 --> 22:35.937
cause I'm running out of patience

22:36.605 --> 22:38.398
lost in distorted thoughts

22:38.482 --> 22:42.360
I can't help but hold my breath

22:42.444 --> 22:44.571
blurred mind, spinning in place

22:44.654 --> 22:46.782
I long to turn away from that scene
to close my eyes.

22:46.865 --> 22:48.033
I don't like what I'm seeing

22:48.116 --> 22:48.950
and it's a curse

22:49.034 --> 22:51.161
it's a thorn in my side

22:52.496 --> 22:54.664
Countless eyes and voices

22:54.748 --> 23:01.463
clapping and laughing,
with a nihilistic air

23:01.546 --> 23:03.632
I'm losing my mind

23:03.715 --> 23:06.176
Inside this scary little world

23:06.259 --> 23:11.056
life is gradually soaking up my dopamine

23:11.139 --> 23:12.516
but I can breathe

23:12.599 --> 23:14.142
I can feel like I matter

23:14.226 --> 23:16.186
in my twisted imagination

23:16.269 --> 23:18.688
cause realitYhurts

23:18.772 --> 23:23.527
I think I'd rather stay here

23:28.573 --> 23:33.453
I think I'd rather stay here
